 a  sequel to one of their hit games much  less a sequel to a smash hit zelda game  and it's also not the first time  nintendo has used a code word in the  place of their zelda video game sequel  name in order to keep the suspense alive  and you'd be right because that's  exactly what they did with what is  perhaps the most famous zelda sequel  majora's mask originally when the first  zelda came out in the ripe year of 1987  the arcade legends massive success  prompted miyamoto and the crew to come  up with a direct sequel to the original  and since it was the second game it was  appropriately announced as and called  zelda 2 with the subtitle the adventure  of link not much suspense here but fast  forward past a couple zelda games in  1991 and 1993 and eventually we were  gifted with the legend of zelda ocarina  of time the greatest game of all time  in my opinion anyway ocarina of time was  another huge smash hit and obviously  following suit with what they did in the  wake of zelda's massive success a decade  earlier they decided once again to make  a direct sequel only this time they used  a code word when announcing the game for  some reason one year after ocarina of  time was gifted to the world in may of  1999 the japanese gaming magazine  famitsu declared that nintendo had  another zelda expansion planned that  would utilize the nintendo 64's 64 dd  storage expansion and this mysterious  project was code named ura zelda which  roughly translates to the hidden zelda  or zelda behind  and one month later in june nintendo  themselves announced that a playable  demo of something called zelda gaiden  would be playable at the nintendo space  world exhibition in august originally  most people and media outlets assumed  that ura zelda and zelda gaiden were one  of the same because of the code names  and the fact that they were announced  merely a month apart from one another  but according to some ign and game  informer articles from 1999 miyamoto  confirmed in august of 99 that the two  were actually separate projects then in  march of y2k nintendo officially  announced that zelda gaiden's actual  name was the legend of zelda majora's  mask with ura zelda assumedly being  eventually released as the ocarina of  time master quest but that's debatable  depending on who you talk to anyway i  recapped all of that to say that  nintendo has famously kept sequels of  major zelda games under the wraps of  code names before but with two big  differences to what they're doing now  with breath of the wild too in the first  place the official name majora's mask  was revealed to the public less than a  year after it was announced under the  code name zelda gaiden now it is true  that nintendo was rushing the game for  other reasons that i won't go into at  this time but even so they announced the  name of the new zelda game before the  hype began to die down which  unfortunately is a bit of what we're  seeing these days with breath of the  wild sequel since you know it's been two  and a half years and all and nintendo  knows this because this isn't their  first rodeo with a sequel in this very  game series so letting the hype die  feels deliberate which leads me to the  second bigger and more mysterious  difference which is that they actually  did tell us why we don't know the name  just yet in an interview with ign this  year nintendo of america's senior  marketing manager bill trynan said that  the name hasn't been announced yet  because it would give too much away and  that's it that's all they said but see  this is why the lack of a name is so  weird to me because let me ask you a  question when have you ever bought a  zelda game or any game for that matter  without knowing the title of said game  and when you knew the title did it give  anything important away about the game  itself i mean sure titles like ocarina  of time kind of spoil the fact that  there's an ocarina of time in the game i  guess and a title like breath of the  wild spoils the fact that link has no  toothbrush to cure his wild breath with  but are either of these or any of the  zelda titles actually spoiling anything  of significance about the story twilight  princess minish cap the wand of gamelon  in each case we're still left like 99.9  in the dark about what's going to happen  in the game but that's just it see since  the game itself hasn't been experienced  yet it doesn't matter what the zelda  game is called because you don't know  what it relates to yet take majora's  mask for example before you play the  game if you read that title you know  that there's a mask that belongs to an  individual named majora but who's majora  you don't know in skyward sword there's  a sword pointing towards the sky but why  does that even matter in literally every  zelda game up until now because the  point of reference for the title is from  within the game itself before you've  played the game you therefore cannot be  spoiled right so bringing this back to  breath of the wild 2 since we really  don't know much about the game itself  there's only one remaining reason as to  why nintendo would consider the title a  spoiler and that would be if it pertains  to something we already know logically  speaking that's the only reason they  would consider it a spoiler and be  afraid of people reading too much into  it so this begs the question what is the  name about well speaking honestly  there's no way we could possibly nail  that down for sure but i think we can  narrow it down to a set number of  possibilities based on what little we do  know about the sequel it's true that the  vast majority of what we've been shown  about the sequel to breath of the wild  is completely mysterious to all of us so  far but there are some things that we've  seen that we can relate to the first  possibility is that it spoils something  about the timeline as a whole namely the  end of the timeline it's no secret that  breath of the wild's timeline placement  has long been debated amongst fans since  it kind of alludes to having taken place  in all of the timelines at different  points in the game but one thing is for  sure it is the most futuristic zelda  game on the timeline meaning it takes  place after all the others regardless of  which specific timeline it is within and  since this new game is going to be a  sequel not prequel to breath of the wild  logically it will then be the new most  futuristic zelda game but that alone is  not the spoiler what would be a spoiler  is if it implied that as the latest game  in the timeline it was also the last  which could be assumed for several  different reasons if it were named  something like the legend of zelda the  end of time or the curse's end or the  last battle or something similar i could  see that giving quite a bit away about  the story of the game or at least just  enough so that fans like me would go  crazy with theories the second  possibility is that it would imply  something about a certain beloved  returning villain that we've seen in the  game so far ganondorf think about it  from everything we know about the sequel  the only thing so far that attaches it  to the older games other than breath of  the wild is ganondorf and we have  several reasons to believe that this is  going to be possibly his biggest and  most notable appearance since ocarina of  time since ganondorf has been the most  recurring villain across the entire  series it makes sense that he's one of  the most recognizable zelda characters  of all time and his appearance in a new  game alone is enough to bring levels of  hype that you've never seen before case  in point the trailer for breath of the  wild 2 there was not a single shot in  that trailer that was revealed to us by  accident and ganondorf's appearance in  both trailers obviously indicates that  he's going to be a huge part in the game  since this is a widely accepted  assumption across the fanbase it would  therefore be a spoiler if the title were  to reveal something about ganondorf  perhaps similarly something about his  end or final appearance in the series  something like the end of the demon king  or ganon's demise  that one has some implications so anyway  to recap everything i've said in this  video i think the fact that nintendo has  been holding out on revealing the name  to us for literally years at this point  and the fact that they said it contains  spoilers about the sequel means that  logically it can only be about one of  two things the timeline or ganondorf i'm  pretty sure that if it were named  something about literally anything else  in the entire game like revenge of the  stone taluses we'd be completely in the  dark but of course that's just my theory  what do you guys think is the sequel to  breath of the wild going to be named  something that gives away a spoiler  about the structure of the zelda  timeline as a whole or perhaps even the  big man himself or is it something else  entirely and nintendo is just holding  out on us for the giggles let me know in  the comments below also thank you so  much for watching please consider  leaving a like below if you liked the  video and to get it spread around to  another zelda fan just like you and me  and subscribe if you haven't already for  lots of videos to come about your  favorite games that's all i've got for  this one so as always i hope you have a  wonderful rest of your day this is mass  intended bandit looking forward to  seeing you next time and signing out  peace  [Music]  you

